    "Style": 112,
    "Text": "The IBM PCjr is a home computer produced and marketed by IBM from March 1984 to May 1985. It was intended as a lower-cost variant of the IBM PC, with hardware capabilities better suited for video games, in order to compete more directly with other home computers such as the Apple II and Commodore 64. It retained the IBM PC's 8088 CPU and BIOS interface, but provided enhanced graphics and sound, ROM cartridge slots, built-in joystick ports, and an infrared wireless keyboard. "
